<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:59:56 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU releases €6.6 billion for members arming Ukraine as seven killed in Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-releases-%E2%82%AC6-6-billion-for-members-arming-ukraine-as-five-killed-in-kyiv</link><description>
European Union countries have agreed to release €6.6 billion from a fund meant to reimburse member states that have  provided arms to Ukraine, EU foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said on Friday. At least seven people were killed in Russian strikes on Kyiv earlier in the day, according to local authorities.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe988e5c-b8fe-11f1-afb5-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26250532034091.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe988e5c-b8fe-11f1-afb5-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26250532034091.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4334d120-b8fe-11f1-a714-b382b43b6a2f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:09:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe988e5c-b8fe-11f1-afb5-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26250532034091.jpg">© Mindaugas Kulbis, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU vows to pursue €120 million fine on X after US backs Musk's court challenge</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-vows-to-pursue-%E2%82%AC120-million-fine-on-x-after-us-backs-musk-s-court-challenge</link><description>
The European Union on Friday said it will pursue a €120 million fine against the X social network after the US Justice Department said it supported the efforts of X owner Elon Musk to have the case annulled. The bloc fined the platform in 2025 for breaching EU online transparency rules, notably with its pay-to-play blue "verification" checkmark. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f01d8900-b8e9-11f1-b5cc-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24047480894574.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f01d8900-b8e9-11f1-b5cc-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24047480894574.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed11161a-b8e8-11f1-bb3d-b9621680640d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:01:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f01d8900-b8e9-11f1-b5cc-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24047480894574.jpg">© Darko Vojinovic, AP</source><dc:creator><![CDATA[FRANCE 24 & FRANCE 3]]></dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>'Moldova is the best performer in my class': EU Enlargement Commissioner Marta Kos</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-moldova-is-the-best-performer-in-my-class-eu-enlargement-commissioner-marta-kos</link><description>
The EU has gone through seven waves of enlargement since 1973, but there has not been one since Croatia joined in 2013. Indeed, there are not likely to be any new members in the club before 2028 – some 15 years after Croatia entered. But 2026 undeniably has momentum, and is on track to be a record year in terms of opening and closing new chapters for existing applicants. That is why our guest, EU Enlargement Commissioner Marta Kos, sees this as "the year of the enlargement."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d2fcbc4-b68c-11f1-b9a5-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/ENTK-TALKING-EU1-KOS-260926-2027-Ep-4-Video-Mixdown-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d2fcbc4-b68c-11f1-b9a5-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/ENTK-TALKING-EU1-KOS-260926-2027-Ep-4-Video-Mixdown-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">16152196-b69b-11f1-a89f-d9af4bfcb869</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:54:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>Climate breakdown: Is the EU adapting to the new normal? Europe's summer of disasters</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-climate-breakdown-is-the-eu-adapting-to-the-new-normal-europe-s-summer-of-disasters</link><description>
It has been called Europe's disaster year. 2026 has seen more than 30,000 excess deaths linked to heatwaves, along with mega wildfires, nuclear power plants having to shut down, gas plants under pressure, droughts reducing hydropower generation from rivers and wild fluctuations in electricity prices, not to mention major disruptions to crops and farming in general.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/988f8e92-b69e-11f1-bca5-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/Debate-heatwave.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/988f8e92-b69e-11f1-bca5-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/Debate-heatwave.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">db72727a-b69d-11f1-9e95-09468f3766b5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:33:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trump made ‘final decision’ to allow Ukraine to produce Patriot missiles, Zelensky says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-trump-made-final-decision-to-give-ukraine-patriot-licence-zelensky-says</link><description>
President Donald Trump told President Volodymyr Zelensky that he had made a "final decision" to grant Kyiv the licence to produce Patriot air defence missiles, the Ukrainian leader said Friday. The assurance came during the last meeting between the two leaders, Zelensky said, capping a period of uncertainty after a series of reversals on the issue.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dae10fc-b8c3-11f1-92c1-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266056109006.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dae10fc-b8c3-11f1-92c1-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266056109006.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">16058bd4-b8c4-11f1-86f7-110fe1281c4e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:46:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dae10fc-b8c3-11f1-92c1-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266056109006.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Revisited</category><title>From 'Jungle' to jungles, migrants in Calais continue to dream of UK</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260925-from-jungle-to-jungles-migrants-in-calais-continue-to-dream-of-uk</link><description>
October 2026 marks 10 years since the Calais "Jungle" in northern France was dismantled by French police. The camp was home to thousands of migrants who wanted to cross the Channel and reach the UK. A decade on, migrants continue to dream of reaching British shores and the "Jungle" has been replaced by many smaller jungles scattered along the northern French coastline. FRANCE 24's Pauline Godart, Claire Paccalin and Mohamed Farhat report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4033b46e-b813-11f1-a6d5-41bcac5946c5/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-calais-EN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4033b46e-b813-11f1-a6d5-41bcac5946c5/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-calais-EN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bed0d594-b828-11f1-ac0c-11ee5c0bceef</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:30:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Pauline GODART</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Pope Leo XIV’s visit to France: What you need to know</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-pope-leo-xiv-s-visit-to-france-what-you-need-to-know</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV on Friday arrives in France for a four-day visit – his fifth Apostolic journey since becoming pontiff last year – during which he hopes to repair the Catholic Church’s standing after sexual abuse scandals while also addressing issues such as the need to regulate AI. FRANCE 24 guides you through his visit.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35a69936-b8b2-11f1-8a8a-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26158300202811.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35a69936-b8b2-11f1-8a8a-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26158300202811.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">591c83d8-b8b4-11f1-8aff-a5a425d3942e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:50:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35a69936-b8b2-11f1-8a8a-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26158300202811.jpg">© Bernat Armangue, AP/ File picture</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'Most powerful force is human potential': Ukraine's military prioritises new tactics, technologies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260925-our-most-powerful-force-is-human-potential-ukraine-military-prioritises-new-tactics-technologies</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Kyrylo Berkal, Deputy Commander of Ukraine's Third Army Corps. He sees Ukraine’s struggle centred on human potential, adaptation and will. While Ukraine is outnumbered, outgunned and sometimes outflanked, their answer is to make human initiative a weapon: giving soldiers and sergeants room to innovate, developing technology from the tactical level upward, and trying to outthink their adversary. Berkal says that Operation Vivaldi embodies that philosophy. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa889388-b8dc-11f1-93dd-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17144992336ab66989b60567-18037487.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa889388-b8dc-11f1-93dd-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17144992336ab66989b60567-18037487.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65f112e4-b8b0-11f1-9c07-11cef6dc51b7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:11:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Pope Leo finishes first day of France tour with youth vigil at Paris stadium</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-live-pope-france-first-state-visit-18-years</link><description>
An estimated 80,000 people welcomed Pope Leo XIV to the Stade de France stadium in Saint-Denis near Paris on Friday. The pontiff warned earlier in the day that an AI "paradise of machines" risked undermining humanity in a speech at the Élysée presidential palace. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/307c2aca-b916-11f1-8d79-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C9EA99K.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/307c2aca-b916-11f1-8d79-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C9EA99K.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1c36588a-b883-11f1-8512-29ef1d31ca1d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:57:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/307c2aca-b916-11f1-8d79-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C9EA99K.jpg">© Alberto Pizzoli, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Schism with rebel Catholic sect casts a pall over Pope Leo’s visit to France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-schism-ultra-conservative-rebel-sect-sspx-pope-leo-visit-france-catholics-lourdes</link><description>
The Vatican’s recent excommunication of followers of a Catholic splinter sect, the Society of Saint Pius X, has revived a longstanding feud within the Roman Catholic Church ahead of Pope Leo XIV’s state visit to France. The ultra-conservative group has established an extensive network of schools and has attracted thousands of followers in France. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/344a7888-b7f8-11f1-a0d8-712f76118fd1/w:1024/p:16x9/visuel-pape-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/344a7888-b7f8-11f1-a0d8-712f76118fd1/w:1024/p:16x9/visuel-pape-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">026e0664-b81f-11f1-a4a1-9f2dc1d15612</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:18:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/344a7888-b7f8-11f1-a0d8-712f76118fd1/w:1024/p:16x9/visuel-pape-2.jpg">© Studio graphique FMM</source><dc:creator>Bahar MAKOOI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU sanctions Russian pundit Xenia Fedorova after expulsion from France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-eu-sanctions-russian-pundit-xenia-fedorova-after-expulsion-from-france</link><description>
The European Union on Thursday imposed sanctions on Russian commentator Xenia Fedorova, whom France expelled in August over claims that she was disseminating "pro-Russian narratives" in the country. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/93eabc96-ad3d-11f1-ad28-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7WQ6KE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/93eabc96-ad3d-11f1-ad28-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7WQ6KE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fbdf6ede-b81c-11f1-916c-817a3a3dabaf</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:45:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/93eabc96-ad3d-11f1-ad28-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7WQ6KE.jpg">© Xavier Galiana, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘Massive, maximum destruction’: Putin seeks to bring Ukrainian civilians ‘to their knees’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/massive-maximum-destruction-putin-seeks-to-bring-ukrainian-civilians-to-their-knees</link><description>
Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev from Kyiv, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative. According to Zalmayev, Russia’s ongoing attacks on Ukraine reflect a broader political logic in which military force, political objectives and territorial ambitions are intertwined as instruments of Russian strategy. He argues that Moscow’s attacks on civilian infrastructure are designed to exert extreme pressure on Ukrainian society while demonstrating fierce retaliation to domestic audiences in Russia. Zalmayev contrasts this with Ukraine’s strikes on Russian energy infrastructure, which he describes as targeting assets that directly sustain Moscow’s war effort.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ab80351e-b80c-11f1-a806-f161c0c5ea55/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-203121-203652-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ab80351e-b80c-11f1-a806-f161c0c5ea55/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-203121-203652-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2a3ce50-b80c-11f1-a30a-ffee22c7666e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:17:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia slams Kyiv with ballistic missiles as Ukrainians brace for harsh winter</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-as-moscow-steps-up-attacks-kyiv-residents-brace-for-harsh-winter</link><description>
Russia on Thursday hit Kyiv with ballistic missiles and drones, killing two people, while a strike on a farm in the Kharkiv region killed six, according to Ukrainian officials. As autumn approaches, Ukrainians are bracing for a tough winter following Moscow's intensifying attacks on the country's energy infrastructure. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/346ad0e8-b7d9-11f1-a926-4d7b41827f6c/w:1024/p:16x9/5801d2697df6a923e557161acb9c00fee897e464.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/346ad0e8-b7d9-11f1-a926-4d7b41827f6c/w:1024/p:16x9/5801d2697df6a923e557161acb9c00fee897e464.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3541a000-b7d9-11f1-bccb-1901ce1b1e6f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 05:31:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/346ad0e8-b7d9-11f1-a926-4d7b41827f6c/w:1024/p:16x9/5801d2697df6a923e557161acb9c00fee897e464.jpg">© Anatolii Stepanov, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: Ukrainian President Zelensky addresses the UN General Assembly</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-ukrainian-president-zelensky-addresses-the-un-general-assembly</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky urged the world’s leaders Wednesday to keep choking Russia’s revenues and impede its war efforts, telling the UN General Assembly that “Russia’s revenues must remain a target”. Watch his full speech above. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/04703e78-b77f-11f1-9a98-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-195330-201931-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/04703e78-b77f-11f1-9a98-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-195330-201931-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">09b0ebda-b77f-11f1-942c-13835db5e770</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 19:44:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky accuses Putin of using nationals of 47 countries to fight Ukraine war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260923-putin-using-citizens-from-47-countries-to-fight-ukraine-zelensky-tells-un</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky told the UN General Assembly on Wednesday that Russian President Vladimir Putin had enlisted fighters from 47 countries including North Korea, Ghana and India to fight against Ukraine. Zelensky also warned that his forces could target Russian heating and energy facilities in the winter months if Moscow continues to attack Ukraine's energy infrastructure.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a98f242-b782-11f1-acc3-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266647906867.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a98f242-b782-11f1-acc3-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266647906867.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">13904f1e-b780-11f1-a29c-43d2500850d4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:53:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a98f242-b782-11f1-acc3-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266647906867.jpg">© Heather Khalifa, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Europe lifts sanctions against two Russians</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe-lifts-sanctions-against-two-russians</link><description>
The EU has agreed to remove Russian billionaires Alisher Usmanov and Mikhail Fridman from its sanctions list, while extending restrictions on nearly 3,000 individuals and companies linked to Russia’s war in Ukraine for another three years. The decision came after difficult negotiations, as EU sanctions require unanimous approval from all 27 member states. Caroline Baum reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef89f844-b726-11f1-a45d-4d220c210a04/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-090753-090927-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef89f844-b726-11f1-a45d-4d220c210a04/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-090753-090927-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f54f87c6-b726-11f1-9009-9dbacafd3f48</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:26:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Azerbaijan pardons jailed Frenchman after EU lifts sanctions on Russian billionaires</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260923-azerbaijan-pardons-jailed-frenchman-after-eu-lifts-sanctions-on-russian-oligarchs</link><description>
Azerbaijan's President ​Ilham Aliyev on Wednesday pardoned a ​French national imprisoned for espionage a day ​after ‌the ⁠EU lifted sanctions on two Russian billionaires. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3cf478e-b722-11f1-8a14-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26202440573121.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3cf478e-b722-11f1-8a14-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26202440573121.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">62764d8e-b723-11f1-b74b-cddd5b8ec36a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 07:53:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3cf478e-b722-11f1-8a14-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26202440573121.jpg">© Ebrahim Noroozi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky says Ukraine is ready for an energy ceasefire with Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-zelensky-says-ukraine-is-ready-for-an-energy-ceasefire-with-russia</link><description>
On the sidelines of the UN General Assembly in New York on Tuesday, Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky told journalists that Kyiv is ready to halt strikes on Russian energy infrastructure if Moscow does the same, with hopes to end the war before winter.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fc1ad66-b6cd-11f1-9bea-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-22T185321Z-294428292-RC2IONAPQIAG-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY-ZELENSKIY-TRUMP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fc1ad66-b6cd-11f1-9bea-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-22T185321Z-294428292-RC2IONAPQIAG-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY-ZELENSKIY-TRUMP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e66bd57e-b6cd-11f1-98a4-f92bcbda5e96</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:38:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fc1ad66-b6cd-11f1-9bea-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-22T185321Z-294428292-RC2IONAPQIAG-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY-ZELENSKIY-TRUMP.jpg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Viral NATO video falsely framed as 'war propaganda' against Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/viral-nato-video-falsely-framed-as-war-propaganda-against-russia-1</link><description>
A viral NATO video is being falsely framed online as "war propaganda", with users accusing the Alliance of sharing a "promotional video" designed to prepare the public for imminent war with Russia. But the footage is not new: NATO published it in July 2024 for its 75th anniversary, and it's been stripped of its original context. The claim comes as European leaders warn of growing Russian hybrid threats, including alleged drone, cyber and sabotage activity. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2579b26c-b6c5-11f1-a667-4d220c210a04/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15120144666ab2e68f813325-23240503.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2579b26c-b6c5-11f1-a667-4d220c210a04/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15120144666ab2e68f813325-23240503.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08e656c8-b6c5-11f1-bcbe-6f1c77cf4e2d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 20:44:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>How is the EU responding to record fuel prices?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-how-is-the-eu-approaching-record-fuel-prices</link><description>
Fuel prices have hit record highs across Europe in recent days, driven by soaring oil prices amid the war in the Middle East and Ukrainian strikes on Russian refineries. However, the scale of the increases, as well as the measures taken to address them, varies significantly from one EU country to another. Here’s why.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a788ff72-b69f-11f1-8f8a-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/7f50b136c93ac6ca88a6c611851705ecc2fc34fb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a788ff72-b69f-11f1-8f8a-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/7f50b136c93ac6ca88a6c611851705ecc2fc34fb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8d012bc-b69f-11f1-aae4-29f34d7893a5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 16:07:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a788ff72-b69f-11f1-8f8a-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/7f50b136c93ac6ca88a6c611851705ecc2fc34fb.jpg">© Alain Jocard, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ladin: Dolomites villages refuse to give up on ancient language</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-ladin-dolomites-villages-refuse-to-give-up-on-ancient-language</link><description>
Year after year, the mountains of the Dolomites become more popular with tourists. Amid millions of visitors, 30,000 inhabitants speak a language only they understand: Ladin, one of the oldest minority languages in Europe. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95696006-b5c4-11f1-bde2-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/TN-PANNEAU-ELENA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95696006-b5c4-11f1-bde2-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/TN-PANNEAU-ELENA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a14619fc-b29d-11f1-8799-01b081c75e09</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 13:30:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95696006-b5c4-11f1-bde2-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/TN-PANNEAU-ELENA.jpg">© ENTR</source><dc:creator>Elena POMPEI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Greenland agreement 'doesn't really give the US many more rights', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260922-greenland-agreement-doesn-t-really-give-the-us-many-more-rights-expert-says</link><description>
As the US, Denmark and Greenland itself sign an agreement on Greenland's security, we've been asking what difference it will actually make. Our expert says the deal won't really give the US many more rights, but that US President Donald Trump wanted to prevent at all costs the tiny risk of Greenland turning towards China. He adds that for Trump voters, if you inflate the risk, people will talk about it and see you're acting. We spoke in Perspective to Mikaa Blugeon-Mered, Senior Researcher on Hydrogen and Arctic Affairs at the Canada Research Chair in Clean Hydrogen at the University of Québec Trois Rivières.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/816fea02-b673-11f1-8b80-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8640513086ab25d97164463-88773820.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/816fea02-b673-11f1-8b80-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8640513086ab25d97164463-88773820.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">463b7f08-b666-11f1-b21b-7dfa233bdef3</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:07:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>First New York, now Berlin: Why the left turn for major metropolises?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260922-first-new-york-now-berlin-why-the-left-turn-for-major-metropolises</link><description>
There's the inroads of the far right, but also the broader desire for change. Introducing Berlin's answer to Zohran Mamdani: Elif Eralp, who led the far-left Die Linke party's historic win in Sunday's municipal elections in Berlin. We ask if the 45-year-old daughter of Turkish political exiles can push through her promises of rent freezes and nationalisation of private real estate companies. Just like in New York last year, affordable housing was a hot-button issue. It didn't hurt that her party ran a social media-savvy campaign.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f7feb3a-b5e8-11f1-9cad-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T165634Z-360619873-RC24NNADN54W-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-BERLIN-LINKE-REACTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f7feb3a-b5e8-11f1-9cad-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T165634Z-360619873-RC24NNADN54W-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-BERLIN-LINKE-REACTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b7df62c8-b5e4-11f1-b1d9-f14263dd641d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 07:56:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK and US make first-ever torpedo test from uncrewed vessel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-uk-and-us-make-first-ever-torpedo-test-from-uncrewed-vessel</link><description>
The United Kingdom and the United States have for the first time test-fired a torpedo from an uncrewed underwater vessel, the UK government said Monday, marking a step forward in AUKUS efforts to develop autonomous naval technology.
